.TH GPAPERD 1 2026-11-14 "gpaperd 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gpaperd \- rotate GNOME light and dark wallpapers
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gpaperd
.RB [ \-\-config
.IR FILE ]
.br
.B gpaperd check\-config
.RB [ \-\-config
.IR FILE ]
.br
.B gpaperd
.RB ( \-\-help | \-\-version )
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gpaperd
is a user daemon that rotates the wallpaper of GNOME's light style and of
its dark style, each from its own list of folders, files and
.B http(s)
URLs.
.PP
In the default
.B slots
apply mode it writes the background keys
.B picture\-uri
and
.B picture\-uri\-dark
once, pointing them at two files it owns,
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/gpaperd/slots/light
and
.IR .../slots/dark .
A rotation atomically replaces the content of a slot with
.BR rename (2);
gnome\-shell's own file monitor then reloads the background.
No key is written during rotation, so GNOME Shell 51 keeps one cached texture
per slot instead of one per image shown.
With
.B apply_mode = \(dquri\(dq
each rotation writes the image's own
.B file://
URI to the keys instead.
.PP
Only the style on screen rotates, unless
.B rotate_hidden
is set; the interval counts the time a style is on screen.
Deadlines are wall-clock instants on a
.B timerfd
on
.BR CLOCK_REALTIME ,
so a change that fell due during suspend happens right after resume,
and a clock step re-arms the timer.
.PP
Each style has a catalog that inotify keeps current (or a poll, for network
and FUSE file systems and with a
.B poll
period).
An image is checked just before use: it must exist, its magic bytes must be
an image, and glycin, the sandboxed loader that gnome-shell uses, must
decode it.
Where glycin's sandbox cannot start, the magic bytes alone decide.
Random order is a shuffle bag: every image once per round.
Alphabetical order is a natural, case-insensitive sort on the file name.
.PP
Remote images are downloaded into
.IR $XDG_CACHE_HOME/gpaperd/remote .
A cached copy is used at once and revalidated in the background; no
rotation waits for the network.
.PP
When something else changes a background key, for example the user picks a
wallpaper in Settings, the
.B on_external_change
policy decides; by default the affected style pauses until
.BR "gpaperctl resume" ,
a config reload, or the key points at the slot again.
.PP
The config file is reloaded when it changes, including through a symlink
into a dotfiles repository.
An invalid edit is logged with line and column and the running config stays.
See
.BR gpaperd.toml (5).
.PP
.B gpaperd
owns the session bus name
.B io.github.worxbend.Gpaperd1
and serves the control interface that
.BR gpaperctl (1)
uses.
A second instance finds the name owned, tells systemd it is ready, so that a
.B Type=notify
unit simply goes inactive instead of being restarted, and exits 0.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B check\-config
Load the config file as the daemon would, scan each local source and look
each URL up in the remote cache, print one line per source, and exit.
A local source line gives the number of image files found by name and
lists what the scan skipped; a URL line says whether the cache holds a copy.
URLs are printed without credentials or query.
It talks to neither GNOME nor the session bus, and creates no slot, state
file, cache entry or directory, so it can run in dotfile CI.
It does not decode images: a counted file may still be rejected at run time.
A source that does not exist is not an error.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-config " FILE"
Read
.I FILE
instead of
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/gpaperd/config.toml .
Accepted before or after
.BR check\-config .
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Stopped by
.B SIGTERM
or
.BR SIGINT ,
another instance already runs, or
.B check\-config
found the config valid.
.TP
.B 1
Any other failure.
.TP
.B 66
.RB ( check\-config
only) The config file does not exist.
The daemon itself runs idle without one and starts when it appears.
.TP
.B 69
Not a GNOME session: the
.B org.gnome.desktop.background
schema is missing, or GSettings uses a backend that does not persist
.RB ( GSETTINGS_BACKEND=memory ).
.TP
.B 78
The config file cannot be read or is invalid; the message has line and
column.
.PP
The systemd unit lists 69 and 78 in
.BR RestartPreventExitStatus= :
a restart cannot help.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.BR SIGTERM ", " SIGINT
Send
.B STOPPING=1
to systemd, save the state and exit 0.
.SH SYSTEMD
Run it as a
.B Type=notify
user service bound to
.BR graphical\-session.target .
.B READY=1
follows the config load, the GNOME check and the first apply, which uses the
images saved in the state file, so a large folder does not delay it.
Before the first apply
.B gpaperd
extends the start timeout by up to five minutes.
.B STATUS=
carries a one-line summary: the style on screen, the image in each slot,
the next change and each paused style.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B HOME
Required. Expands
.B \(ti
in the config.
.TP
.BR XDG_CONFIG_HOME ", " XDG_DATA_HOME ", " XDG_STATE_HOME ", " XDG_CACHE_HOME
Base directories, with the XDG fallbacks under
.BR HOME .
.TP
.BR HTTP_PROXY ", " HTTPS_PROXY
Proxy for downloads. GNOME's own proxy settings are not read.
.TP
.B JOURNAL_STREAM
When it names stderr, logs go to the journal with the fields
.BR STYLE= ,
.BR ITEM= ,
.BR METHOD= ,
.B REASON=
and
.BR PATH= .
Otherwise logs go to stderr.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/gpaperd/config.toml
The config file; see
.BR gpaperd.toml (5).
.TP
.IR $XDG_DATA_HOME/gpaperd/slots/light ", " .../slots/dark
The slot files the background keys point at.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/gpaperd/state.json
Current images, bags, cursors, deadlines, pauses, history and the user's
original background keys.
.TP
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/gpaperd/remote/
Downloaded images, one directory per URL.
.TP
.I ~/.config/systemd/user/gpaperd.service
The user unit, shipped as
.IR dist/gpaperd.service .
.SH EXAMPLES
Check a config from a dotfiles repository in CI:
.PP
.RS
.EX
gpaperd check\-config \-\-config gpaperd/config.toml
.EE
.RE
.PP
Follow the log:
.PP
.RS
.EX
journalctl \-\-user \-u gpaperd \-f
.EE
.RE
.SH NOTES
Slot mode relies on gnome-shell reloading a background file that is
replaced by
.BR rename (2).
The source code says it does, but it has not yet been verified on a live
GNOME 50 or 51 session.
If the wallpaper does not change on rotation, set
.B apply_mode = \(dquri\(dq
in the config.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gpaperctl (1),
.BR gpaperd.toml (5),
.BR systemd.service (5),
.BR gsettings (1)
